    <name>
      <text>Evaluating Logarithmic Expressions</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Evaluate correct to 6 decimal places</p>
<p>\(\log_{@random_num2@}{@random_num1@}=\) [[input:ans1]][[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>\(\log_{@random_num3@}{@float(random_num/10)@}=\) [[input:ans2]][[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>(a)  \(\displaystyle \log_{@random_num2@}{@random_num1@}=x \Longleftrightarrow {@random_num2@}^x={@random_num1@} \)</p>
<p>\( \displaystyle \Longleftrightarrow \ln {@random_num2@}^x=\ln {@random_num1@} \Longleftrightarrow x \ln {@random_num2@} =\ln {@random_num1@} \)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \Longleftrightarrow x=\frac{\ln {@random_num1@}}{\ln {@random_num2@}}\)</p>
<p>Thus, \( \displaystyle \log_{@random_num2@}{@random_num1@}=\frac{\ln{@random_num1@}}{\ln{@random_num2@}} \approx {@ta1@}...\)</p>
<p>(b)  \(\displaystyle \log_{@random_num3@}{@float(random_num/10)@}=y \Longleftrightarrow {@random_num3@}^y={@float(random_num/10)@} \)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \ln{@random_num3@}^y=\ln {@float(random_num/10)@} \Longleftrightarrow y \ln {@random_num3@} =\ln {@float(random_num/10)@} \)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \Longleftrightarrow y=\frac{\ln {@float(random_num/10)@}}{\ln{@random_num3@}}\)</p>
<p>Thus,  \(\displaystyle \log_{@random_num3@}{@float(random_num/10)@}=\frac{\ln {@float(random_num/10)@}}{\ln{@random_num3@}} \approx {@ta2@}...\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
